<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Statistical processing</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the Central Limit Theorem (CLT), the distribution of the user request means should converge to a normal distribution. This allows us to calculate the benchmark mean and <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95\%</annotation></semantics></math> confidence interval across all 600 user request means. However, since the user request augmentation was based on the 60 original user requests, traditional i.i.d. assumptions required for the CLT to hold are weakened. To account for this, we use the clustered standard error adjustment when calculating the confidence interval.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Formally, let <math id="A6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the request-level score (mean of <math id="A6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=10</annotation></semantics></math> trials at <math id="A6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=0.7</annotation></semantics></math>) for request <math id="A6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>600</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=600</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}</annotation></semantics></math> be the mean across the <math id="A6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> requests. We define the index clusters <math id="A6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1,\dots,60" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1,\dots,60</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in c</annotation></semantics></math> if user request <math id="A6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> comes from the original user request <math id="A6.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. The standard error according to the CLT can be calculated as</p>
<table id="A6.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{SE}_{\text{CLT}}=\sqrt{\frac{1}{n(n-1)}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(s_{i}-\bar{s})^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>SE</mtext><mtext>CLT</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{SE}_{\text{CLT}}=\sqrt{\frac{1}{n(n-1)}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(s_{i}-\bar{s})^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The clustered standard error adjustment (<math id="A6.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{SE}_{\text{clustered}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>SE</mtext><mtext>clustered</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{SE}_{\text{clustered}}</annotation></semantics></math>) can be calculated as</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A6.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{SE}_{\text{clustered}}=\sqrt{\text{SE}_{\text{CLT}}^{2}+\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{c=1}^{60}\sum_{i\in c}\sum_{j\in c,j\neq i}(s_{i,c}-\bar{s})(s_{j,c}-\bar{s})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>SE</mtext><mtext>clustered</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mtext>SE</mtext><mtext>CLT</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>60</mn></munderover><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{SE}_{\text{clustered}}=\sqrt{\text{SE}_{\text{CLT}}^{2}+\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{c=1}^{60}\sum_{i\in c}\sum_{j\in c,j\neq i}(s_{i,c}-\bar{s})(s_{j,c}-\bar{s})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For all models, we report the mean score together with standard and clustered <math id="A6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95\%</annotation></semantics></math> confidence intervals as <math id="A6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}\pm 1.96\text{ SE}_{\text{clustered}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>1.96</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext> SE</mtext><mtext>clustered</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}\pm 1.96\text{ SE}_{\text{clustered}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}\pm 1.96\text{ SE}_{\text{CLT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>1.96</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext> SE</mtext><mtext>CLT</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}\pm 1.96\text{ SE}_{\text{CLT}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Injected System Prompt</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<div id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx196" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
